In the `NODE_CASE` handling:
```c
while (n) {
  codegen(s, n->car, VAL);  // generate code for when value
  if (head) {
    gen_move(s, cursp(), head, 0);
    push(); push(); pop(); pop(); pop();
    ...
  }
  else {
    pop();
  }
  tmp = genjmp2(s, OP_JMPIF, cursp(), pos2, NOVAL);
  pos2 = tmp;
  n = n->cdr;
}
```

After `codegen(s, n->car, VAL)`, the value is on the stack. Then `gen_move(s, cursp(), head, 0)` moves the value to the `head` register. Then `push(); push(); pop(); pop(); pop()` - this pushes 2 and pops 3, net -1. Then `genop_3(s, OP_SEND, cursp(), ...)` - this sends a message with 1 argument, which pops the receiver and argument and pushes the result.

So after the `when` value is processed, `cursp()` is roughly the same as before. The `genjmp2` is called with `cursp()` which is the current stack pointer.

